{
  "schema_version": "fabric.sandbox-id-vectors/v1",
  "rule": "Spec 056 §4.3 rule H5, §7.3.3 (a) and (b): container and pod ids. cgroups: the eBPF emitter (hostrecords.SandboxIDs) reads the kernfs names of a sandbox-scope event's cgroup and its parent (last_two); the container id comes from the leaf, else the parent: docker-, cri-containerd-, crio- or libpod- + 64 lowercase hex + '.scope', or exactly 64 lowercase hex; the pod uid from kubepods[-<qos>]-pod<uid>.slice ('_' read as '-') or pod<uid>. The full path and last_two give the same ids. outputs: the exec hook (WP6-08) derives fabric.sandbox.created_id from one simple command (argv, or a shell string shlex.split turns into one with no ;, &, |, &&, ||, <, > token; argv[0] by basename) and its standard output with one trailing newline removed: docker, podman or nerdctl run with -d/--detach (also --detach=true and a short-flag cluster holding d, read up to the image: the first token that is neither an option nor the value of an option in value_options), or create (container run/create too), printing exactly 64 lowercase hex -> container:<hex>; kubectl run, create or apply with -o jsonpath={.metadata.uid} (-o X, -oX, -o=X, --output X, --output=X; one pair of quotes around the template removed) printing exactly a lowercase UUID, or with -o json printing a JSON object of at most 1 MiB whose kind is Pod and metadata.uid a lowercase UUID -> k8s-pod:<uid>. clear null: no id. ids and created_id are sbx- v2 of the clear text under the key; both sides use the same key, so they match.",
